From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:50:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: host CADCraft in an Intuition window through egui-aros

apps/cadcraft-aros is the desktop app's counterpart on AROS: CadApp runs in one Intuition window through egui-aros (winit and egui-winit for the window and input, the CPU renderer or OpenGL chosen at run time with --gui-renderer or the GUI_RENDERER ToolType, ASL requesters, the system clipboard's text). Start-up data (Workbench arguments, ToolTypes, the program's drawer, absolute document names) comes from egui-aros too; this crate has no unsafe code.

The workspace file, settings, autosave files, the LISP support folder and the log live in CADCraftData in the program's drawer. The program runs in the -nix path mode and converts names at the requesters. The loop has no idle poll. The drawing area is drawn through egui: the wgpu canvas is not set up. Not here: the control server, the DWG worker process, 3D mice, the self-updater and a native window per floating panel. --screenshot and --test-steps are test aids.
